# The registered wildcard arms over dtype-carrying enums, one line per
# enclosing function: `path function-name reason`. A wildcard not listed here
# fails check_dtype_wildcards.py — register it with its reason, or make the
# match exhaustive. Adding a dtype makes this file the review list: every line
# below is a place a new variant falls into silently, and its reason says why
# that was safe for the variants that existed when it was written. Re-read the
# reason, not just the line, when the variant set grows.
frame/pivot.mbt widen_unpivot_cell documented invariant — the unify raised unless the cells pass through unchanged
internal/column/builtin.mbt BuiltinColumn::from_scalars off-type cell projects to null; the outer DataType match is the compile-forced gate
internal/kernel/date.mbt eval_dt_date_component the dtype gate above leaves only Date, Timestamp and Null cells; the wildcard is the null
internal/kernel/date.mbt eval_dt_clock_component the dtype gate above leaves only Timestamp and Null cells; the wildcard is the null
internal/kernel/predicate.mbt try_fast_is_in fast path declines to the general Scalar-comparing path for buffers it does not accelerate
internal/kernel/predicate.mbt hash_set_is_in non-Null members go through key_of, which declines the fast path for an off-type member
series/null.mbt Series::fill_null the inner gate raises TypeMismatch (loud); the outer Scalar match is exhaustive
series/row_gather.mbt Series::gather_series fast path declines to rebuild_by_row for buffers it does not accelerate
series/series_stats.mbt Series::mean the reducer's result contract is Float|Null; the wildcard arm is the raise
series/series_stats.mbt Series::std the reducer's result contract is Float|Null; the wildcard arm is the raise
series/series_stats.mbt Series::variance the reducer's result contract is Float|Null; the wildcard arm is the raise
series/series_stats.mbt Series::median the reducer's result contract is Float|Null; the wildcard arm is the raise
series/series_stats.mbt Series::quantile the reducer's result contract is Float|Null; the wildcard arm is the raise
internal/column/storage.mbt <top> the wildcard is exhaustiveness only — the dtype identity check above already answered every mixed pair (same dtype implies same variant), so no cell comparison runs here
# Binding-name catch-all arms (`other =>`) and closure-parameter lines that
# lead a line inside a dtype match block (`i => ...`) register here exactly
# like `_` arms — the guard treats every spelling of "catches the rest" the
# same.
examples/sales_analysis/pipeline/pipeline.mbt is_widget_row the catch-all reads a present cell's as_string; the null arm above it is the example's point
frame/dataframe.mbt typed_column_cells the catch-all decodes the cell or raises TypeMismatch — a new variant is refused, never silently coerced
frame/null.mbt DataFrame::fill_null the catch-all compares dtypes (fills only when the scalar's dtype matches the column's) — a new variant simply does not fill
frame/null.mbt DataFrame::fill_nan the catch-all is the identity pass-through: only Float cells carry NaN, every other variant rides unchanged
frame/pivot.mbt reshape_pivot the catch-all renders the cell for the pivot card — a new variant renders by its own to_string, as today's do
internal/column/builtin_cast.mbt BuiltinColumn::to_int closure-parameter lines inside the cast's cell loops (i =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
internal/column/builtin_cast.mbt BuiltinColumn::cast_date_to_timestamp closure-parameter lines inside the cast's cell loops (i => / b =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
internal/column/builtin_cast.mbt BuiltinColumn::cast_timestamp_to_date closure-parameter lines inside the cast's cell loops (i => / b =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
internal/column/builtin_cast.mbt BuiltinColumn::to_float closure-parameter lines inside the cast's cell loops (i =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
internal/column/builtin_cast.mbt BuiltinColumn::to_string_column closure-parameter lines inside the cast's cell loops (i =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
internal/kernel/ternary.mbt eval_ternary closure-parameter lines inside the cell selectors (i =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
series/reduce.mbt reduce_present closure-parameter lines inside the fold drivers (k => / i =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
series/reduce.mbt reduce_arith closure-parameter lines inside the fold drivers (k =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
series/reduce.mbt numeric_double_reader closure-parameter lines in the reader arms' bodies (i =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
series/reduce.mbt reduce_arg_extremum closure-parameter lines inside the extremum drivers (k => / (x, y) =>), not match arms — the scanner is deliberately lexical
series/reduce.mbt reduce_arg_extremum the Bool order arm names its own comparator ((x, y) => …), a bare-binding line the scanner reads as a catch-all; the arm is exhaustive over Bool
series/series.mbt typed_cells the catch-all decodes the cell or raises TypeMismatch — a new variant is refused, never silently coerced
types/scalar.mbt Scalar::as_int the catch-all routes every other variant to expected_type's loud TypeMismatch raise — a new variant is refused, never silently coerced
types/scalar.mbt Scalar::as_float the catch-all routes every other variant to expected_type's loud TypeMismatch raise — a new variant is refused, never silently coerced
types/scalar.mbt Scalar::as_bool the catch-all routes every other variant to expected_type's loud TypeMismatch raise — a new variant is refused, never silently coerced
types/scalar.mbt Scalar::as_string the catch-all routes every other variant to expected_type's loud TypeMismatch raise — a new variant is refused, never silently coerced
series/series.mbt Series::from_i64_options the wildcard passes the non-decimal riders through — Int and the date-likes carry no envelope to check, and a new rider decides its own spelling here at compile time
types/error.mbt json_cell_expectation the catch-all derives the diagnostic wording from the variant itself ("a Duration"), so a new variant renders correctly with no behaviour to swallow — the signature half of the attribution rule caught this arm, whose bare-variant arms carry no enum spelling
io/json_core.mbt frame_from_json_records the wildcard rejects a non-object JSON record with a located ParseError — the scrutinee is a Json value, not a dtype enum; the signature's dtypes parameter triggered the signature-half attribution
internal/parquet/build.mbt build_series the page walk fixes one Scalar variant per column's map; the wildcard is the null cell (and any off-type cell the walk nulls)
internal/parquet/write.mbt encode_plain_value the map fixes the (physical, scalar) pair; the wildcard raises loudly — a cell the map cannot carry refuses the write
internal/parquet/read.mbt decode_column the arms route by page type and encoding; the wildcards are the null cells and the off-type cells the def levels null
internal/parquet/read.mbt decode_plain_values the catch's wildcard is the malformed-UTF-8 raise — the loud refusal, not a silent swallow
internal/kernel/temporal.mbt temporal_arith the cell match is over the temporal pairs; the wildcard is the null (or mixed) source pair — one per the date and the shift half
